@crew bakshi-sol
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Bakshi. Helm, nights. Hold still a second. No reason. Well, a small reason.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Turn left at that last star and we'd be somewhere warm by now.
- {hi}. Hold still. No, the other side. Thanks. That's your nose done.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I plotted a course to your home. Just to see. It's a nice route.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good night at the helm. The stars went past very politely.
? mood:low
- Bit grey today. I painted rain. Didn't help. Nice painting, though.

== near
? act:work
- Course steady. I've a second one plotted for fun. It goes nowhere. It's lovely.
? act:leisure
- Common room's quiet. Good light in here for painting. Very small paintings.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I grew up on Lisk. It rained every day. I complained every day. Now I miss it.
? tier>=colleague
- Tiny portraits keep turning up on bunks. Some are mine. I'm not saying which.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- On rest days I plot courses to places we'll never go. Want to pick one?

== about
? aff:dlamini-lukas:friend
- Lukas and I stand in the garden when the misters run. It smells like home. Both our homes.   #warm
